{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1903, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given an N \\times N grid S and an M \\times M grid T. The cell at the i-th row from the top and the j-th column from the left is denoted by (i,j).\nThe colors of the cells in S and T are represented by N^2 characters S_{i,j} (1\\leq i,j\\leq N) and M^2 characters T_{i,j} (1\\leq i,j\\leq M), respectively. In grid S, cell (i,j) is white if S_{i,j} is ., and black if S_{i,j} is #. The same applies for grid T.\nFind T within S. More precisely, output integers a and b (1 \\leq a,b \\leq N-M+1) that satisfy the following condition:\n\n- S_{a+i-1,b+j-1} = T_{i,j} for every i,j (1\\leq i,j \\leq M).\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN M\r\nS_{1,1}S_{1,2}\\dots S_{1,N}\r\nS_{2,1}S_{2,2}\\dots S_{2,N}\r\n\\vdots\r\nS_{N,1}S_{N,2}\\dots S_{N,N}\r\nT_{1,1}T_{1,2}\\dots T_{1,M}\r\nT_{2,1}T_{2,2}\\dots T_{2,M}\r\n\\vdots\r\nT_{M,1}T_{M,2}\\dots T_{M,M}\n\nOutput\n\nPrint a and b in this order, separated by a space on one line.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq M \\leq N \\leq 50\n- N and M are integers.\n- Each of S_{i,j} and T_{i,j} is . or #.\n- There is exactly one pair (a,b) satisfying the condition.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n3 2\r\n#.#\r\n..#\r\n##.\r\n.#\r\n#.\n\nSample Output 1\n\n2 2\r\n\nThe 2 \\times 2 subgrid of S from the 2nd to the 3rd row and from the 2nd to the 3rd column matches T.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n2 1\r\n#.\r\n##\r\n.\n\nSample Output 2\n\n1 2\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1955, "char_start": 1915, "quote": "Input:\n3 2\n#.#\n..#\n##.\n.#\n#.\nOutput:\n2 2", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1997, "char_start": 1967, "quote": "Input:\n2 1\n#.\n##\n.\nOutput:\n1 2", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "ce6624981a26b9552d8168961a37aae5406f3793d93817c2cf20df5f401adc60", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "bd99eeb8f24bc69e2e03bb9531056080b25cdd0c24686769e73cf15d04d88052", "seq": 2}
